</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our data is sourced from AgentGym <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xi et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. Following practice in previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bengio et al., 2009</a>; <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mukherjee et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, we categorize the tasks <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> into <em id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">easy</em> and <em id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hard</em> difficulty levels (denoted as <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\text{easy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mtext>easy</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\text{easy}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\text{hard}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mtext>hard</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\text{hard}}</annotation></semantics></math>) based on the <span id="A2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">avg@8</span> results of the Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct model, while ensuring a balanced distribution of data between the two difficulty levels. The same categorization is applied to the test set.
Detailed statistics for each environment are provided in Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Dataset Details ‣ Can RL Improve Generalization of LLM Agents? An Empirical Study" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
