<td id="A2.T5.5.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">55</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="145" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">145</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">145</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.6.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T5.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">BabyAI</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="398" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">398</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">398</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="412" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">412</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">412</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="810" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">810</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">810</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">52</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="38" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">38</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">38</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.5.7.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">90</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Detailed algorithm of GRPO.</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) is an efficient online reinforcement learning algorithm tailored for LLMs. It eliminates the need for a separate critic network typically required in PPO, thereby reducing computational overhead. Instead, GRPO estimates the baseline using <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">group relative advantages</span> to significantly reduce gradient variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, for each input query <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (derived from <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>), GRPO samples a group of outputs <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from the old policy <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> and obtains their corresponding rewards <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{1},R_{2},\dots,R_{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{1},R_{2},\dots,R_{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The advantage <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each output is calculated by normalizing the rewards within the group:</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{R_{1},\dots,R_{G}\})}{\text{std}(\{R_{1},\dots,R_{G}\})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{R_{1},\dots,R_{G}\})}{\text{std}(\{R_{1},\dots,R_{G}\})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, GRPO updates the policy by maximizing the following surrogate objective, which incorporates PPO-style clipping <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite> and a KL divergence penalty to ensure training stability:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)={}\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Big(\min\!\big(r_{i}(\theta)A_{i},\;\text{clip}\big(r_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\big)A_{i}\big)-\beta\mathbb{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}\Big)\Bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)={}\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Big(\min\!\big(r_{i}(\theta)A_{i},\;\text{clip}\big(r_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\big)A_{i}\big)-\beta\mathbb{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}\Big)\Bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|q)}{\pi_{\theta_{old}}(y_{i}|q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|q)}{\pi_{\theta_{old}}(y_{i}|q)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability ratio between the new and old policies, <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the outputs <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> sampled from the old policy <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math> given the query <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the clipping parameter, and <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the coefficient for the KL divergence term.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed Results of Sequential Cross-Environment Training</h2>

<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.12011v1/performance_3x4.svg" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/211;" width="476" height="211"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A4.F7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training dynamics of forgetting and transfer in other sequential two-stage cross-environment training with Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, where <span id="A4.F7.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#4E6691;">blue</span> and <span id="A4.F7.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B8474D;">red</span> denote the upstream environment and the downstream environment, respectively.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S6.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 6.0.0.1 Setting. ‣ 6 How Does Sequential RFT Across Environments Affect Transfer and Forgetting? ‣ Can RL Improve Generalization of LLM Agents? An Empirical Study" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in Section <a href="#S6" title="6 How Does Sequential RFT Across Environments Affect Transfer and Forgetting? ‣ Can RL Improve Generalization of LLM Agents? An Empirical Study" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> illustrates the training dynamics for 8 two-stage sequential training configurations. Here, we present the dynamics for the remaining 12 pairs in Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results of Sequential Cross-Environment Training ‣ Can RL Improve Generalization of LLM Agents? An Empirical Study" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. Additionally, detailed final results are reported in Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results of Sequential Cross-Environment Training ‣ Can RL Improve Generalization of LLM Agents? An Empirical Study" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A4.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results of sequential training across different environments with Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct model.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T6.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T6.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Upstream</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Downstream</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">WebShop</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">SearchQA</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">TextCraft</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">AlfWorld</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">BabyAI</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.5.2" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="A4.T6.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">base model</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" alttext="28.59" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathsize="0.900em">28.59</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">28.59</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" alttext="31.19" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathsize="0.900em">31.19</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.19</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" alttext="33.63" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathsize="0.900em">33.63</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">33.63</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" alttext="26.56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathsize="0.900em">26.56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26.56</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" alttext="67.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathsize="0.900em">67.00</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">67.00</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
